<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Duchy of Moscow</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Muscovite</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, or Muscovy, was the Russian principality that rose from the fourteenth century to dominate the Rus' lands and throw off Mongol overlordship. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> it expanded greatly, and it became the core of the Tsardom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p></div>
